{
    "background_story": "Stetson was a rugged cowboy who spent his life riding the open ranges of the American West. Growing up on a ranch, he developed a strong constitution and an unsusceptibility to the harsh elements. Whether it was a scorching desert sun or a freezing mountain blizzard, Stetson faced each challenge with a stoic determination. His immune system was equally resilient, shrugging off illnesses that would fell a lesser man. When a deadly influenza outbreak swept through the territory, Stetson remained healthy, nursing his fellow cowhands back to health. His toughness and unsusceptibility earned him the nickname 'The Iron Horse,' a testament to his unyielding spirit and physical hardiness. Stetson's legend grew, and he became a symbol of the American frontier's unbreakable spirit.",
